<div class="hero-section py-5 service-page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row align-items-center min-vh-50">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto text-center">
        <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3" style="font-size: clamp(28px, 4.5vw, 52px); line-height: 1.15;" data-page-h1>
          Route planning and proof-of-service platform for Shoreline Waste
        </h1>
        <p class="mb-0" style="font-size: clamp(16px, 2vw, 18px); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 980px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.95);">
          A full stack logistics and telematics platform that modernizes dispatching, proves service completion, and optimizes routes in real time without disrupting daily operations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="inner-sections">

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="problem">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row g-4 align-items-start">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-7">
          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center heading-left mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">The problem</h2>
          <p class="large-para mb-3">
            A regional waste management provider relied on static, legacy route sheets. Drivers frequently deviated from optimal paths, fuel costs were unmonitored, and missed pick up disputes were unresolvable due to lack of visual evidence.
          </p>
          <p class="large-para mb-0">
            The goal was to modernize fleet operations without disrupting daily proof of service requirements. &ldquo;Close enough&rdquo; routing doesn&rsquo;t work at scale: exceptions are constant (blocked bins, on call adds), and without GPS verified proof of work, customer claims turn into refunds and operational churn.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-5">
          <%= render "home/case_studies/at_a_glance",
            industry: "Logistics / waste hauling",
            client: "Shoreline Waste",
            country: "United States",
            what_we_built: "Route planning, live dispatch, geofence-verified proof of service, billing triggers",
            integrations: "Google Maps Fleet Engine, Samsara/Geotab, Stripe",
            stack: "React Native, Node.js microservices, PostgreSQL + PostGIS" %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="what-we-built">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">What we built</h2>
        <p class="large-para mb-3">
          A full stack logistics and telematics platform that uses AI to solve route sequencing in real time, paired with a ruggedized mobile app for field execution.
        </p>
        <p class="large-para mb-0">
          Dispatchers get an AI route planner and live fleet visibility; drivers get a low friction workflow that captures proof of work at the right moment. Proof of service is built into the operational loop, and completion events can trigger billing automatically, keeping dispatch, finance, and customer support synchronized.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-white" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">How it works</h2>
        <ul class="service-page-list mb-4" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8;">
          <li><strong>Heuristic routing:</strong> Google Maps Fleet Engine recalculates routes based on real time traffic, vehicle constraints, and service window SLAs.</li>
          <li><strong>Geofence verification:</strong> Photo capture triggers only when GPS intersects the customer&rsquo;s service polygon to produce defensible proof of work.</li>
          <li><strong>Architecture:</strong> React Native (mobile) → Node.js microservices → PostgreSQL + PostGIS.</li>
          <li><strong>Integrations:</strong> Samsara/Geotab for engine diagnostics; Stripe for automated pay-per-lift billing.</li>
          <li><strong>Reliability:</strong> Event driven route updates, idempotent job completion events, queue backed photo and billing processing, RBAC and audit trails.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="large-para mb-0">
          Designed for missed stops, blocked bins, on-call pickups mid route, offline-first driver workflows, and dispatch changes that must reach drivers instantly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey" id="results">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="col-12 col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">Results</h2>
        <ul class="service-page-list mb-0" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8;">
          <li><strong>Lower fuel waste</strong> through optimized stop sequencing, reduced idling, and constraint aware routing.</li>
          <li><strong>Automated dispatching</strong> reduced manual route planning through reliable route generation and exception handling.</li>
          <li><strong>Fewer disputes</strong> resolved faster via GPS verified photos and audit ready proof of service.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%= render "home/case_studies/gallery", slug: "shoreline-waste-logistics" %>
  <%= render "home/case_studies/client_quote", slug: "shoreline-waste-logistics" %>
  <%= render "home/case_studies/cta", blurb: "We’ll map the operations workflow, real time data flows, and reliability requirements, then ship in phases without disruption." %>

  <section class="py-4 bg-white">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <%= link_to "Operations-heavy software →", industry_professional_services_path, class: "service-card-link ajax" %>
      <% if route_helper_defined?(:industry_logistics_path) %>
        <span class="text-muted mx-2">·</span>
        <%= link_to "Logistics →", industry_logistics_path, class: "service-card-link ajax" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
